T&#x0003e;550 &#x000b5;m.</p><p>IOP=intraocular pressure; GAT=Goldmann applanation tonometry; DCT=dynamic contour tonometry; CCT=central corneal thickness.</p><p>Statistically significant <italic>p</italic> values are marked with asterisk (<sup>*</sup>).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Relationship of IOP measured by GAT and DCT with CCT in left eyes assessed by multivariate regression morel</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjo-23-27-i003"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Group A: CCT&#x0003c;520 &#x000b5;m; Group B: 520 &#x000b5;m &#x02264; CCT &#x02264; 550 &#x000b5;m; Group C: CCT&#x0003e;550 &#x000b5;m.</p><p>IOP=intraocular pressure; GAT=Goldmann applanation tonometry; DCT=dynamic contour tonometry; CCT=central corneal thickness.</p><p>Statistically significant <italic>p</italic> values are marked with asterisk (<sup>*</sup>).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>